  "description": "Reid Method 1 | 20\" BMX Bike\nBuilt for young riders ready to get into BMX, the Reid Bikes Method 1 is a tough and capable 20\" BMX bike for kids aged 7+ years. Designed for BMX parks, pump tracks, street spots and everyday riding, it provides a solid platform for learning new skills and building confidence.\nThe Hi-Ten steel frame features modern BMX geometry for predictable handling and responsive control. A 20.75\" top tube, compact rear end and 8.6\" riser bars create a comfortable setup for young riders learning manuals, stalls, jumps and other BMX skills.\nA radius U-brake with a two-finger lever provides reliable control, while Kenda 2.25\" street tyres deliver grip across different riding surfaces. Stunt pegs are included, giving riders the option to practise tricks and develop their skills.\nBuilt to handle the demands of BMX riding, the Reid Bikes Method 1 features a forged alloy stem and seat clamp, 36-hole rims and a durable KMC chain. Finished in black with a clean BMX-inspired look, it's ready for riders looking to start their BMX journey.\nWho is the Reid Bikes Method 1 for?\nThe Method 1 BMX is ideal for:\n\nKids aged 7+ years starting out in BMX\nYoung riders learning BMX skills and tricks\nBMX parks, pump tracks and street riding\nRiders practising manuals, stalls and jumps\nBeginners looking for a tough and reliable BMX bike\nRiders wanting a BMX with stunt pegs included",
